 Medium\n9\tcreated_date: \"2026-11-07\"\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t# Implement the /sc:pr-submit merge guard (issue #375)\n13\t\n14\tSource: ./source.md\n15\tGoal: With `/sc:pr-submit --monitor 3`, a PR is turned into a draft as soon as a verified Medium-or-higher finding is routed to a fix, and is marked ready again only when that cycle's fix push is confirmed on the PR head (or a zero-edit cycle is proven), with every failure, override, crash, resume and exit path leaving the PR in a known, reported state.\n16\t\n17\t## Constraints\n18\t\n19\t- Edit canonical files under `src/superclaude/` only, then run `make sync-dev`; do not stage `.claude/` mirror files. Use UV for every Python command (`uv run pytest ...`, `uv run ruff ...`).\n20\t- The new pure module `src/superclaude/pr_submit/merge_guard.py` and every file already listed in `CORE_PURE_FILES` of `tests/pr_submit/test_static_grep.py` (including `refs/state-machine.md` and `refs/loop-guard.md`) must contain no whole word `gh` or `git` on any line, comments included. The module must not import `recovery` (an import cycle through `run_log`).\n21\t- Protocol and command text must not contain the string `src/superclaude`; `SKILL.md` must keep exactly one python code fence; edits to `SKILL.md` and `refs/state-machine.md` are additive sentences, bullets and rows placed after, never inside, the sentences pinned by `tests/pr_submit/test_static_grep.py` and `tests/pr_submit/test_conflict_sync_protocol.py`. A new `SKILL.md` line must not name `evidence-validator` or `conflict-intent.md` (a line-content test allows those words only on lines that also say \"Tier 2\") and must not use wording that the forbidden-force-push line test rejects; Task 1 lists the exact line-content rules before any edit.\n22\t- Every new line under `src/superclaude/skills/`, `src/superclaude/commands/` or `src/superclaude/agents/` that contains `gh pr`, `gh api` or a git write verb needs one entry in `WRITE_VERB_CLASSIFICATION` in `tests/skills/test_worker_contract.py` (key: repo-relative path, verb text, exact stripped line; category `never-worker` with the standard pr-submit reason text of the neighbouring entries). Add each entry last in the task that writes the file, because editing a classified line later makes the entry stale and fails `test_classification_table_has_no_stale_entries`; run `uv run pytest tests/skills/test_worker_contract.py -q` in that task.\n23\t- Cite tests and constants by symbol name (for example `_NEW_KEY_DEFAULTS`, `_RESOLUTION_SCRIPTS`, `CORE_PURE_FILES`, `WRITE_VERB_CLASSIFICATION`), never by line number, in plan text, task artifacts and the protocol prose this plan produces. Protocol prose carries no `file:NNN` pointers.\n24\t- No test or task may call GitHub. Script tests use a fake `gh` executable on `PATH`. The behaviour that needs a disposable fork PR (gates G1 live part, G2 live part, G4, G5 and G6 of ./source.md section 8) is recorded as OPEN and is a release gate, never claimed verified.\n25\t- Scope limits (non-goals of ./source.md): no labels, commit statuses or rulesets; ordinals 0 to 2 change only by one report line; conflict-merge cycles (Tier 1 and Tier 2) are never engaged; the guard is not held through re-review or CI; a second concurrent run on the same PR is unsupported.\n26\t- Owner decisions already accepted (listed in the ./source.md header and section 8) are fixed: draft not label; engage at the end of Wave 3; default on at `--monitor 3`; release on the confirmed push before replies and the re-trigger; unreadable timeline or unpublished exit keeps the PR draft; build now with no GitHub calls, release gate for G4 and G5.\n27\t- Run `make sync-dev` at the end of every task that edits a file under `src/superclaude/skills/` or `src/superclaude/commands/`, because the full test suite runs `make verify-sync` through `tests/cli/test_verify_sync_hooks.py`.\n28\t\n29\t## Phase 1: Contracts and pure core\n30\t\n31\t## Task 1: Write the pre-build record `./artifacts/pre-build-gate.md`\n32\t\n33\tCreate `./artifacts/pre-build-gate.md` in this package from ./source.md sections 6, 8 and 10. First record the base-commit state: run `make lint`, `uv run ruff format --check src/ tests/` and the full suite `uv run pytest -q tests` before any code edit and write each exit code, the pass count and every failing test id (or \"clean\") into the file, so later failures can be told apart from this feature's. Then record the release-gate decision of ./source.md section 8 in the owner's words: the build proceeds with no GitHub calls (fake `gh` in tests); gates G1 (live part), G2 (live part), G4, G5 and G6 are a release gate that the owner runs on a disposable fork PR before the feature is merged or turned on by default; the user guide states that draft behaviour is unverified until then; the PR body states the gate plainly; the run that opens the PR must pass `--merge-guard off`. Then close the open items by reading the code: O1, where `src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/SKILL.md` (Wave 3 to Wave 6 and Wave 8 text) and `refs/loop-guard.md` assign a fix or CI cycle's `cycle_id` today and whether any test under `tests/pr_submit/` pins a value; O2, how scripts are granted and invoked in the SKILL front matter and what `test_allowed_tools_cover_every_program` in `tests/pr_submit/test_conflict_sync_protocol.py` and the `_RESOLUTION_SCRIPTS` tests in `tests/pr_submit/test_static_grep.py` require of a new script; O3, every exact-text pin and line-content rule (for example `test_intent_and_validator_lines_say_tier_2`, `test_skill_forbids_force_push`, the wait-only sentences pinned for `refs/state-machine.md`, and the `WRITE_VERB_CLASSIFICATION` table with its stale-entry test in `tests/skills/test_worker_contract.py`) on `SKILL.md`, `refs/state-machine.md`, `refs/loop-guard.md` and `src/superclaude/commands/pr-submit.md` that the later additive edits must avoid; O4, that the S5a re-trigger sentence in `SKILL.md` stays unchanged and where the new