t_guard_requested` and `draft_guard_settled`, without the whole words `gh` or `git` (the file is in `CORE_PURE_FILES`). Update `tests/pr_submit/test_run_log.py` (the test `test_eventtype_is_43_members_with_silence_reviewer_and_conflict_events`: rename it to describe 45 members, assert both lengths are 45 and both new values are present) and the `len(EventType)` assertion in `tests/pr_submit/test_codex_reviews.py` to 45. Leave `tests/pr_submit/test_idempotency.py` (7 sets) unchanged. Run `make sync-dev`.\n45\t\n46\tAcceptance criteria:\n47\t- `uv run pytest tests/pr_submit/test_run_log.py tests/pr_submit/test_codex_reviews.py tests/pr_submit/test_idempotency.py tests/pr_submit/test_static_grep.py -q` passes with `len(EventType) == 45` and the two new values asserted.\n48\t- `RunLog.append` accepts an event with `event_type: \"draft_guard_requested\"` and still rejects an unknown type, with the updated count in the error message.\n49\t- `grep -rn \"43\" src/superclaude/pr_submit/models.py src/superclaude/pr_submit/run_log.py src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/refs/loop-guard.md` shows no remaining claim that the enum has 43 members, and `refs/loop-guard.md` names both new event values.\n50\t- `make verify-sync` exits 0 after the sync.\n51\t\n52\t## Task 3: Create `merge_guard.py` types, cycle ids, fold, pending matcher, published check and status mapping\n53\t\n54\tDepends on: Task 2\n55\t\n56\tCreate `src/superclaude/pr_submit/merge_guard.py` following ./source.md sections 4.1, 4.2 and 4.6: `GuardMode`, `Direction`, `Phase`, `GuardAction`, `GuardRead`, `GuardDecision`; the string constants `BRANCH_LANDED = \"landed\"`, `BRANCH_NOT_LANDED = \"not_landed\"`, `BRANCH_AMBIGUOUS = \"ambiguous\"`; `fix_cycle_id(kind, n)` and `next_cycle_number(events, kind)` (never colliding with `CONFLICT_CYCLE_PREFIXES` from `src/superclaude/pr_submit/conflicts.py`); `fold_draft_guard(events)` implementing every row of the section 4.2 effect table (fields `phase, phase_before_r